": "berkshire", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "gm", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "southwest airlines co.", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "delta air lines inc.", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "phillips", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "general motors co.", "sentiment": "none"}]}, "highlightText": "", "language": "english", "persons": [], "text": "Berkshire Hathaway Inc. (BRKA)(BRKA) said it loaded up on shares of Apple Inc. (AAPL) while trimming its stake in American Airlines Group Inc. (AAL), according to a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission late Tuesday. Berkshire also added to positions of Bank of New York Mellon Corp. (BK), Delta Air Lines Inc. (DAL), Southwest Airlines Co. (LUV), and General Motors Co. (GM). Berkshire reduced its stake in Phillips 66 (PSX), United Continental Holdings Inc. (UAL), and Wells Fargo & Co. (WFC).\n-Wallace Witkowski; 14-18 1657ET\n ", "external_links": ["http://www.addthis.com/bookmark.php?v=250"], "published": "2018-08-14T03:00:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-08-15T05:03:55.002+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}